        "wild": "Thylacoleo furtimorsus is a large marsupial predator that lurks in redwood forests and on cliff faces. It is an ambush hunter, clinging to trees and dropping onto prey from above. Its powerful bite induces a severe bleeding effect that rapidly drains its victim's health. Its retractable claws allow it to cling to vertical surfaces — even zip lines.",
